
  Below the bar are a "12 of 48 events" count in a polite live region and a "Clear filters" button. When nothing
  matches, the table body is replaced by an empty state ("No events match these filters") with the same clear button.
  Changing a control filters right away. It never navigates or submits, and nothing goes into the URL.

  [1mNo JS[0m
  The filter bar markup ships with the [38;5;153mhidden[39m attribute, and the script removes it. With JS off, nobody sees controls
  that can't work. The table itself still needs JS to render. That problem existed before this change and I'm leaving it
  alone unless you want it fixed here.

